# Context

## Why This Way
zodiac-autoresearch was a standalone local git repo (13 commits
on master, no remote). Options were: add it as a gitlink (broken
submodule), drop its history, or absorb it with git subtree.
Subtree won: full history is preserved under the prefix and the
files are plain tracked files, so clones work with no extra
setup.

## Gotchas
- The subtree carries its own .gitignore, which keeps
  results.tsv and run.log untracked by design (append-only run
  artifacts). Override deliberately if you want them published.
- Command used: git subtree add --prefix=zodiac-autoresearch
  <path-to-old-repo> master
